    "result_text": "The full suite (the acceptance test) passes. My implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct membership-level rule with a points system across two layers:\n\n**API contract** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`): Added a new read-only `membershipPoints` field and rewrote `membershipLevel`'s description to derive from those points. Both fields are returned by the owner endpoints (DTOs are generated from this spec at build time).\n\n**Mapping logic** (`OwnerMapper.java`):\n- `resolveMembershipPoints(owner)` \u2014 starts at 0; `+2` for a present email, `+1` when `namesakeCount` is 0, `+2` for a household of 3+ (`getHouseholdSize()`, null-safe), `+3` for tenure over 365 days. Reuses the existing `hasEmail(...)` helper.\n- `resolveMembershipLevel(owner)` \u2014 now just maps points to a level: `1` (0\u20131), `2` (2\u20133), `3` (4\u20135), `4` (6+).\n\nEach method has a single responsibility (level delegates to points rather than duplicating the factor logic), and I introduced named constants `TENURE_POINTS_THRESHOLD_DAYS` and `HOUSEHOLD_POINTS_THRESHOLD` in place of the old level-specific one.\n\nThe acceptance test (`membershipPoints` = 3, `membershipLevel` = 2 for a fresh, single-member-household owner with an email and no namesake) and the full build pass green.",
