    "probe_text": "Here's the complete, ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`. It's handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:104-151`) \u2014 the V2 controller only exposes a paged list, not a create.\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Before the handler runs (framework-level)\n\n1. **Authorization.** `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` \u2014 caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, else the request is rejected.\n\n2. **Request-body bean validation** (`@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`, `OwnersApi.java:85-86`). Per-field constraints on `OwnerFieldsDto`:\n   - **firstName** \u2014 `@NotNull`/`@NotBlank`, `@Size(1,30)`, `@Pattern ^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$` (letters, up to 3 words separated by space/apostrophe/hyphen).\n   - **lastName** \u2014 `@NotNull`/`@NotBlank`, `@Size(1,30)`, `@Pattern ^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$` (as above, optional trailing dot).\n   - **address** \u2014 `@NotNull`/`@NotBlank`, `@Size(1,255)`.\n   - **city** \u2014 `@NotNull`/`@NotBlank`, `@Size(1,80)`.\n   - **telephone** \u2014 `@NotNull`/`@NotBlank`, `@Size(1,20)`, and `@Telephone`: must normalize to E.164 (strip spaces/dashes/brackets, assume `+61` and drop a leading `0` when no `+`, require 8\u201315 digits) **and** pass the per-country national-length rule (`+1` \u2192 10 national digits, `+61` \u2192 9; unknown codes unconstrained).\n   - **email** (optional) \u2014 `@Email`, `@Size(1,255)`, and `@NotDisposableEmail` (rejects disposable-domain addresses).\n   - **Class-level `@ValidPostcode`** \u2014 if a postcode is supplied it must be exactly 4 digits and fall in the range for the city's region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099); a city with no known region accepts any 4-digit postcode; absent postcode is allowed. Violations report against the `postcode` property.\n\n   Note: `sharesHousehold` has no constraint (write-only flag).\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Mapping DTO \u2192 entity (`ownerMapper.toOwner`, normalization side-effects)\n\n`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:108`, rules in `OwnerMapper.java:164-187`:\n\n3. **telephone normalized** to canonical E.164 (`TelephoneNormalizer.toE164`).\n4. **address normalized** (`AddressNormalizer`): trimmed, whitespace collapsed, upper-cased, and abbreviations expanded (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`).\n5. **email lower-cased** via `Owner.setEmail` (`Owner.java:121-123`).\n6. `id`, `pets`, `householdId` deliberately not mapped; `sharesHousehold` not carried onto the entity.\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 Handler business logic (in order)\n\n7. **Future-registration check** \u2014 `isRegistrationDateInFuture`: if a registrationDate was supplied and is after today \u2192 **400 Bad Request** (returns, no save).\n8. **Resolve registration date (side-effect)** \u2014 `resolveRegistrationDate`: null \u2192 today, then `BusinessDay.rollForward` (a weekend rolls to the following Monday). Result set back onto the owner.\n9. **Daily limit check** \u2014 `isDailyOwnerLimitReached`: if owners already registered on that (resolved) date \u2265 100 \u2192 **429 Too Many Requests**.\n10. **City capacity check** \u2014 `isCityAtCapacity`: if owners in that city (case-insensitive count) \u2265 50 \u2192 **409 Conflict**.\n11. **Assign household (side-effect)** \u2014 `assignHousehold`: if a postcode is present, set `householdId` = first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 of `canonical(lastName) + \"|\" + postcode`. No postcode \u2192 left null.\n12. Compute `declaredHouseholdMember` = (`sharesHousehold == true`).\n13. **Household-duplicate check** \u2014 `existsOwnerInHousehold` (an existing owner with same last name (ignore-case) + same postcode) **and not** declared \u2192 **409 Conflict**.\n14. **Exact identity-key duplicate check** \u2014 `existsOwnerWithIdentityKey`: an existing owner sharing the whole identity key `telephone|email|householdId` (looked up among owners with the same telephone) \u2192 **409 Conflict**.\n15. **namesakeCount (side-effect)** \u2014 `countNamesakes`: number of existing owners with same last name (ignore-case) and same first name (ignore-case).\n16. **householdSize (side-effect)** \u2014 `countHouseholdMembers`: existing household members + 1.\n17. **bulkSignupWarning (side-effect)** \u2014 `isBulkSignupWarranted`: true if owners already on that date > 80.\n18. **Possible-duplicate flags (side-effect)** \u2014 only when **not** a declared member: `findPossibleDuplicateOwnerId` finds the lowest-id existing owner with same last name (ignore-case) + same postcode but a *different* telephone; sets `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (that id). (Declared members skip this and leave the flags at their defaults.)\n19. **Save (side-effects)** \u2014 `saveOwner` (`ClinicServiceImpl.java:242-250`):\n    - If the owner is new and has no customerCode, **generate customerCode** = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode via `LocalityResolver`; HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 of `telephone + lastName`).\n    - `ownerRepository.save(owner)` persists it; on persist the entity's `@PrePersist defaultRegistrationDate` (`Owner.java:243-247`) runs again (defaults null \u2192 today and rolls to a business day \u2014 idempotent here since step 8 already did it).\n20. **Audit (side-effect)** \u2014 `ownerAuditor.auditCreated(owner)`: logs `id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate` to the `AUDIT` logger.\n21. **Response mapping** \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto` computes derived fields (displayName, telephoneDisplay, initials, locality, membershipNumber, Luhn checkDigit, membershipPoints, membershipLevel, contactPreference, ageBand, identityKey).\n22. **Location header** set to `/api/owners/{id}`, response returned as **201 Created**.\n\n### Notes on ordering\n- Because the duplicate/limit checks (steps 9, 10, 13, 14) run *after* the registration date is resolved (step 8) and the household id is assigned (step 11), they operate on the resolved/normalized values, not the raw request.\n- Any check that returns early (steps 7, 9, 10, 13, 14) skips all later side-effects, including the save and audit.\n\nNothing was changed \u2014 this is read-only analysis."
